# dotfiles-openSUSE/.env.example
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reference for the environment knobs this layer and its vendored Core respond to.
# .gitignore already carries `!.env.example`, so this file is tracked while any real
# `.env` / `.env.*` is not — but no .env is required or read automatically: nothing
# here sources a dotenv file. This is documentation you can copy from, and the place
# to look before hunting through bootstrap.sh.
#
# Shell knobs belong in ~/.config/zsh/99-local.zsh (host-local, never tracked).
# Bootstrap knobs are passed on the command line: `BLIB_SU=doas ./bootstrap.sh`.

# ── bootstrap.sh ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Privilege escalator. Default `sudo`. Set to "" when already root (minimal
# containers often ship no sudo at all), or to `doas` on a doas-only box.
#BLIB_SU=

# Plan-only mode for Core's link helpers. Set by `./bootstrap.sh --dry-run`;
# you rarely need to set it by hand.
#BLIB_DRY=1

# ── Core shell layer (see core/zsh/loader.zsh) ───────────────────────────────
# Which Core fragment bands load: minimal (<=30), standard (<=50), full (<=69).
# Bands >=70 (the OS layer, role layers, 99-local) always load regardless.
#CORE_PROFILE=full

# Where `notes`-style helpers look. Defaults to ~/Notes.
#NOTES_DIR=

# ── this OS layer (os/opensuse.zsh) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to any non-empty value to stop the auto-attach of a `main` tmux session on
# interactive shells. Useful in containers, CI, and editor-spawned shells.
# Must be set in ~/.zshenv or the environment — NOT in 99-local.zsh, which the
# loader reads after the band-80 OS layer has already run.
#DOTFILES_NO_AUTOTMUX=1

# ── Makefile ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Upstream used by `make core-verify`. Override only if you are working against a fork
# or a local mirror of dotfiles-core.
#CORE_REMOTE=https://github.com/dotgibson/dotfiles-core.git
